    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="1617" n="1577" xml:id="pg1577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/6–1454: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 833<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        the United Kingdom</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d833-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-15T18:19:00-04:00">June 15, 1954—6:19
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6835. Dept believes tripartite powers should make concerted but separate <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarches</hi> to IG re border measures soonest London
                    tel 5714<anchor n="2" xml:id="d833-f2"/> USUN 868.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d833-f3"
                    /></p>
                <p>Powers would be open to valid Israel criticism if they did not present IG with
                    full list measures presented Amman. Since entire matter to be discussed with
                    UNSYG, fact we had differentiated between Israel and Jordan in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> would eventually become known and, coupled
                    with fact Jordan approached first, would reduce possibilities creating receptive
                    and cooperative spirit on part IG re measures. (FYI: Not known how far UK
                    Ambassador Washingon or French Ambassador Tel Aviv have gone in talking with
                    Israelis re border.)</p>
                <p>Do not feel powers should apprise UNSYG re <hi rendition="#italic">démarches</hi>
                    or seek his support for implementation by UN of particular measures until <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> has been made to IG.</p>
                <p>Embs London and Paris should seek soonest and report on UK and French agreement
                    for respective missions in Israel to proceed on above basis.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d833-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d833-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d833-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to Paris priority; repeated to Tel Aviv, Amman, Jerusalem, and New
                    York; sent by pouch to Ankara, Baghdad, Beirut, Cairo, Jidda, and Damascus.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d833-f2" n="2" xml:id="d833-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d832"><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d833-f3" n="3" xml:id="d833-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d833-f4" n="4" xml:id="d833-f4-content">
                <p>Ambassador Aldrich reported on June 17 that the British Foreign Office agreed to
                    a separate but concerned approach to the Israeli Government and to the
                    presentation of a full list of proposed measures. (Telegram 5809 from London,
                    June 17, 6 p.m.: 684A.85/6–1754)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
